doc:sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "187A(4) Service providers must keep certain information and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to be kept:  (a) information that is the contents or substance of a communication; or Note: This paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not required to keep information about telecommunications content.  (b) information that:  (i) states an address to which a communication was sent on the internet, from a telecommunications device, using ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 1  Data retention" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187AA Information to be kept"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187aa ;
    values:originalText "(1) The following table sets out the kinds of information that a service provider must keep, or cause to be kept, under subsection 187A(1):  Kinds of information to be kept Item Topic Column 1 Description of information Column 2 The subscriber of, and accounts, services, telecommunications devices and other relevant services relating to, the relevant service The following: (a) any information that is one or both of the following: (i) any name or address information; (ii) any other information for identification purposes; relating to the relevant service, being information used by the service provider for the purposes of identifying the subscriber of the relevant service; (b) any information relating to any contract, agreement or arrangement relating to the relevant service, or to any related account, service or device; (c) any information that is one or both of the following: (i) billing or payment information; (ii) contact information; relating to the relevant service, being information used by the service provider in relation to the relevant service; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 1  Data retention" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The following table sets out the kinds of information that a service provider must keep, or cause to be kept, under subsection 187A(1):  Kinds of information to be kept Item Topic Column 1 Description of information Column 2 The subscriber of, and accounts, services, telecommunications devices and other relevant services relating to, the relevant service The following: (a) any information that is one or both of the following: (i) any name or address information; (ii) any other information for identification purposes; relating to the relevant service, being information used by the service provider for the purposes of identifying the subscriber of the relevant service; (b) any information relating to any contract, agreement or arrangement relating to the relevant service, or to any related account, service or device; (c) any information that is one or both of the following: (i) billing or payment information; (ii) contact information; relating to the relevant service, being information used by the service provider in relation to the relevant service; ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 1  Data retention"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3854998ff6dcfca3aa0d19ad3ff1a7adcbd1088b85ee8cb6a4870b345eb21381" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Service provider must keep certain information about subscribers and services." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
