doc:sch-1-sec-187g-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "187G(1) Consultation with agencies and the ACMA" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) As soon as practicable after receiving an application under section 187E to approve a data retention implementation plan (the original plan), the Communications Access Co-ordinator must:  (a) give a copy of the plan to the enforcement agencies and security authorities that, in the opinion of the Co-ordinator, are likely to be interested in the plan; and  (b) invite each such enforcement agency or security authority to provide comments on the plan to the Co-ordinator. The Co-ordinator may give a copy of the plan to the ACMA. Request for amendment of original plan" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187G(2) Consultation with agencies and the ACMA"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187g-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If:  (a) the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a comment from an enforcement agency or security authority requesting an amendment of the original plan; and  (b) the Co-ordinator considers the request to be a reasonable one; the Co-ordinator:  (c) must request that the service provider make the amendment within 30 days (the response period) after receiving the comment or summary; and  (d) may give the service provider a copy of the comment or a summary of the comment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  Response to request for amendment of original plan" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If:  (a) the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a comment from an enforcement agency or security authority requesting an amendment of the original plan; and  (b) the Co-ordinator considers the request to be a reasonable one; the Co-ordinator:  (c) must request that the service provider make the amendment within 30 days (the response period) after receiving the comment or summary; and  (d) may give the service provider a copy of the comment or a summary of the comment. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  Response to request for amendment of original plan"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "92393f06aef8be58614295fd0fb8e64bb3c2d010eab3c3ffe0af1026c30c68b2" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187g ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must request amendment within 30 days after receiving comment or summary." ;
    dc:description "Amendment to original plan" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
