concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187K The Communications Access Co-ordinator may grant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187k ;
    values:originalText "exemptions or variations Decision to exempt or vary  (1) The Communications Access Co-ordinator may:  (a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations imposed on the service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period specified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to information or documents that relate to a specified kind of relevant service. A variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the obligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject under sections 187A and 187C.  (2) The decision must be in writing.  (3) The decision may be: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 1  Data retention" ;
    skos:definition "exemptions or variations Decision to exempt or vary  (1) The Communications Access Co-ordinator may:  (a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations imposed on the service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period specified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to information or documents that relate to a specified kind of relevant service. A variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the obligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject under sections 187A and 187C.  (2) The decision must be in writing.  (3) The decision may be: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 1  Data retention"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f478a747a7e686ead2477df7a34501abc780419ea144d8a9b25a8b6a9685fe18" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-3 ;
