concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187L Confidentiality of applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187l ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a service provider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data retention implementation plan, or application for a decision under subsection 187K(1), the Co-ordinator must:  (a) treat the application as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body (other than the ACMA, an enforcement agency or a security authority) without the written permission of the service provider. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  (1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under section 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1), the ACMA must:  (a) treat the application as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body (other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an enforcement agency or a security authority) without the written permission of the service provider.  (2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an enforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives under subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or subsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:  (a) treat the copy as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body without the written permission of the service provider." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Communications Access Co-ordinator receives a service provider’s application under section 187E for approval of a data retention implementation plan, or application for a decision under subsection 187K(1), the Co-ordinator must:  (a) treat the application as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body (other than the ACMA, an enforcement agency or a security authority) without the written permission of the service provider. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  (1A) If the ACMA receives a service provider’s application under section 187KA for review of a decision under subsection 187K(1), the ACMA must:  (a) treat the application as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body (other than the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an enforcement agency or a security authority) without the written permission of the service provider.  (2) The ACMA, the Communications Access Co-ordinator, an enforcement agency or a security authority must, if it receives under subsection 187G(1), paragraph 187K(5)(a) or subsection 187KA(3) a copy of a service provider’s application:  (a) treat the copy as confidential; and  (b) ensure that it is not disclosed to any other person or body without the written permission of the service provider."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bfeb80c190c7020feb0225debadafdacac925a4fe10b9281e0b13af73e6b7c00" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-1a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-187l-ss-2 ;
