concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-1j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1J Subsection 6C(1) (note)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-1j ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the note, substitute: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  Note 1: Under section 187LA of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, service providers are, in relation to their activities relating to retained data, treated as organisations for the purposes of this Act. Note: 2: Regulations may prescribe an instrumentality by reference to one or more classes of instrumentality. See subsection 13(3) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003. Telecommunications Act 1997" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the note, substitute: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  Note 1: Under section 187LA of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979, service providers are, in relation to their activities relating to retained data, treated as organisations for the purposes of this Act. Note: 2: Regulations may prescribe an instrumentality by reference to one or more classes of instrumentality. See subsection 13(3) of the Legislative Instruments Act 2003. Telecommunications Act 1997"@en ;
