    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3C(2) At the end of section 281"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3c-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subject to subsection (3), this section does not apply to a disclosure of information or a document by a person as a witness in a civil proceeding if the information or document:  (a) is kept, by a service provider (within the meaning of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979), ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  solely for the purpose of complying with Part 5-1A of that Act; and  (b) is not used or disclosed by the service provider for any purpose other than one or more of the following purposes:  (i) complying with Part 5-1A of that Act;  (ii) complying with the requirements of warrants under Chapters 2 and 3 of that Act or authorisations under Chapter 4 of that Act;  (iii) complying with requests or requirements to make disclosures provided for by sections 284 to 288 of this Act;  (iv) providing persons with access to their personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988;  (v) a purpose prescribed by the regulations;  (vi) a purpose incidental to any of the purposes referred to in subparagraphs (i) to (v)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subject to subsection (3), this section does not apply to a disclosure of information or a document by a person as a witness in a civil proceeding if the information or document:  (a) is kept, by a service provider (within the meaning of the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979), ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Data retention  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  solely for the purpose of complying with Part 5-1A of that Act; and  (b) is not used or disclosed by the service provider for any purpose other than one or more of the following purposes:  (i) complying with Part 5-1A of that Act;  (ii) complying with the requirements of warrants under Chapters 2 and 3 of that Act or authorisations under Chapter 4 of that Act;  (iii) complying with requests or requirements to make disclosures provided for by sections 284 to 288 of this Act;  (iv) providing persons with access to their personal information in accordance with the Privacy Act 1988;  (v) a purpose prescribed by the regulations;  (vi) a purpose incidental to any of the purposes referred to in subparagraphs (i) to (v)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e5b6aeae88268e1854db32879a8998f46f7e99d158a7e38bd0ab4f8b718f28d7" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-3c ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of information or document by a person as a witness in a civil proceeding is permitted for specific purposes." ;
