concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-6t a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6T Subsection 182(2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-6t ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute: Exempt disclosures  (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing person information if:  (a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under section 185D or 185E; or  (ii) for the performance by the Organisation of its functions; or  (iii) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or  (iv) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty; or  (v) for the protection of the public revenue; or  (b) the disclosure is:  (i) to an IGIS official for the purpose of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security exercising powers, or performing functions or duties, under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986; or  (ii) by an IGIS official in connection with the IGIS official exercising powers, or performing functions or duties, under that Act. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute: Exempt disclosures  (2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing person information if:  (a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:  (i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under section 185D or 185E; or  (ii) for the performance by the Organisation of its functions; or  (iii) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or  (iv) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty; or  (v) for the protection of the public revenue; or  (b) the disclosure is:  (i) to an IGIS official for the purpose of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security exercising powers, or performing functions or duties, under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986; or  (ii) by an IGIS official in connection with the IGIS official exercising powers, or performing functions or duties, under that Act. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a44e02007e00094d12d9a22a88227d60115423fc269adc9558320905d7b5acd1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of non-missing person information is permitted under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf> ;
