doc:sch-1-sec-185d-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "185D(1) Notification etc. of authorisations intended to identify media" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a journalist information warrant is issued under Subdivision B of Division 4C of Part 4-1:  (a) the Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable, give a copy of the warrant to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security; and  (b) the Minister must, as soon as practicable, cause the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security to be notified of the issuing of the warrant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-1-sec-185d-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "185D(2) Notification etc. of authorisations intended to identify media"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-185d-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If an authorisation under Division 3 of Part 4-1 is made under the authority of the warrant, the Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable after the expiry of the warrant, give a copy of the authorisation to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If an authorisation under Division 3 of Part 4-1 is made under the authority of the warrant, the Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable after the expiry of the warrant, give a copy of the authorisation to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security."@en ;
