doc:sch-3-sec-186c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "186C Power to obtain relevant information" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an officer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give information relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records, the Ombudsman may: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Schedule 3  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman" ;
    cof:pageNumber "83"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "186D Ombudsman to be given information and access despite other"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-186d ;
    values:originalText "laws  (1) Despite any other law, a person is not excused from giving information, answering a question, or giving access to a document, as and when required under this Chapter, on the ground that giving the information, answering the question, or giving access to the document, as the case may be, would:  (a) contravene a law; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  (b) be contrary to the public interest; or  (c) might tend to incriminate the person or make the person liable to a penalty.  (2) However:  (a) the information, the answer, or the fact that the person has given access to the document, as the case may be; and  (b) any information or thing (including a document) obtained as a direct or indirect consequence of giving the information, answering the question or giving access to the document; is not admissible in evidence against the person except in a proceeding by way of a prosecution for an offence against section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or against Part 7.4 or 7.7 of the Criminal Code.  (3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:  (a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or in writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or  (b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting officer; for the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records.  (4) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from making a record of information, or causing a record of information to be made, for the purposes of giving the information to a person as permitted by subsection (3)." ;
    skos:definition "laws  (1) Despite any other law, a person is not excused from giving information, answering a question, or giving access to a document, as and when required under this Chapter, on the ground that giving the information, answering the question, or giving access to the document, as the case may be, would:  (a) contravene a law; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00039  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Schedule 3 Amendments  Part 1  No. 39, 2015 Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Amendment (Data Retention) Act 2015  (b) be contrary to the public interest; or  (c) might tend to incriminate the person or make the person liable to a penalty.  (2) However:  (a) the information, the answer, or the fact that the person has given access to the document, as the case may be; and  (b) any information or thing (including a document) obtained as a direct or indirect consequence of giving the information, answering the question or giving access to the document; is not admissible in evidence against the person except in a proceeding by way of a prosecution for an offence against section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or against Part 7.4 or 7.7 of the Criminal Code.  (3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:  (a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or in writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or  (b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting officer; for the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records.  (4) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from making a record of information, or causing a record of information to be made, for the purposes of giving the information to a person as permitted by subsection (3)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8954b4ce200e1b10594592fbed1a8ba405c3e70d3a3ae2909815f7b5cdaf992c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.84" .
