doc:sch-3-sec-186d-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "186D(2) Ombudsman to be given information and access despite other" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However:  (a) the information, the answer, or the fact that the person has given access to the document, as the case may be; and  (b) any information or thing (including a document) obtained as a direct or indirect consequence of giving the information, answering the question or giving access to the document; is not admissible in evidence against the person except in a proceeding by way of a prosecution for an offence against section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or against Part 7.4 or 7.7 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "186D(3) Ombudsman to be given information and access despite other"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-186d-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:  (a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or in writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or  (b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting officer; for the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law, prevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:  (a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or in writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or  (b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting officer; for the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the agency’s records."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e28876e3565e282ab35aa8c702032e33983d3f3db8de203790893ff8e0bc4afa" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "An officer of an enforcement agency must provide information and access to an inspecting officer." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015.pdf, p.84" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-amendment-data-retention-act-2015-sch-3-sec-186d-ss-3-norm .
